---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation — Tether CLI"
  description="Install Tether, connect and trust your machines, and manage dotfiles, packages, package checks, profiles, and team sync."
>
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">YOUR GUIDE TO A CONNECTED ENVIRONMENT</p>
    <h1>Get your machines<br /><em>on the same page.</em></h1>
    <p>Tether syncs dotfiles and global packages across your machines through a Git repository you own. It encrypts dotfiles by default. Package manifests stay readable.</p>
    <p>Each machine signs a record of the packages it installed. A synced package installs on its own only when a machine you trust lists it, and it passes the package checks.</p>

    <h3>What Tether does</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dotfile sync</strong>: AES-256-GCM encryption with a passphrase-protected key</li>
      <li><strong>Package sync</strong>: Homebrew, npm, pnpm, bun, gem and uv</li>
      <li><strong>Package checks</strong>: signed machine records, a release-age limit, OSV malware checks, install scripts off, and a Homebrew tap allowlist</li>
      <li><strong>Profiles</strong>: choose the dotfiles and packages each machine gets</li>
      <li><strong>Background daemon</strong>: syncs every 5 minutes</li>
      <li><strong>Secret detection</strong>: scans team dotfiles for credentials. See <a href="/docs/encryption#secret-detection">Secret detection</a> for the commands that scan</li>
      <li><strong>Teams</strong>: share dotfiles and project secrets with age keys</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Start here</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New to Tether: <a href="/docs/install">Install</a>, then follow the <a href="/docs/quick-start">Quick start</a></li>
      <li>On Tether 1.x: read <a href="/docs/upgrade">Upgrade from 1.x</a> before you upgrade the first machine</li>
      <li>A package does not install: see <a href="/docs/inbox">The Inbox</a> and <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a></li>
      <li>All commands and settings: see <a href="/docs/commands">Commands</a> and <a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    // The docs were one page before 2.0. Old links point to its anchors.
    (function () {
      var moved = {
        introduction: '/docs', installation: '/docs/install', 'quick-start': '/docs/quick-start', upgrade: '/docs/upgrade',
        linux: '/docs/linux', 'how-it-works': '/docs/how-it-works', dashboard: '/docs/dashboard', 'dashboard-keys': '/docs/dashboard#keys',
        commands: '/docs/commands', 'cmd-scripting': '/docs/scripting', configuration: '/docs/configuration',
        'local-config': '/docs/configuration#local-config', 'feature-toggles': '/docs/configuration#feature-toggles',
        'machine-profiles': '/docs/profiles', 'package-profiles': '/docs/profiles#package-profiles', 'profiles-1x': '/docs/profiles#profiles-1x',
        'keep-servers-clean': '/docs/servers', 'package-managers': '/docs/packages', 'package-security': '/docs/package-security',
        'approval-inbox': '/docs/inbox', 'machine-trust': '/docs/trust', 'old-machine-ids': '/docs/trust#old-machine-ids',
        encryption: '/docs/encryption', 'team-sync': '/docs/team-sync', troubleshooting: '/docs/troubleshooting'
      };
      var id = location.hash.slice(1);
      var target = moved[id] || (id.indexOf('cmd-') === 0 ? '/docs/commands#' + id : null);
